<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47750" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tendĭcŭla</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		dim.
		tendo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a little stretcher.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vestimenta tendiculis diducta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 1, 3, 2</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b> ( = fraus), <i>a little
				snare</i>, <i>noose</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aucupia verborum et litterarum tendiculae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Caecin. 23, 65</span></i>
			: verborum tendiculas aucupemur, Ambros. de Fide, 3, 5,
			§ 37; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Prov. 1, 11</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
